   "file": "0005-studio-ui-api-base.patch",
   "sha256": "0442f57fd90c67d49debb32708c12a5fc0310b0971fe00e0ae4e3e6b0a30c62c",
   "purpose": "Studio UI runtime API base (107-fix-3 C11): every runtime /__studio/* URL the native editor builds (session/locales/source/mutation/feedback/artifact/artifact-name/library/material/storyboard/surface-preview) is a root-relative string literal upstream, which resolves against the host origin when the editor is mounted under a per-session vite base (/studio/<sessionId>/ via patch 0001) and never reaches the session proxy (nginx only routes the session prefix; the broker proxy refuses root-relative paths). main.ts's top-level session fetch then fails to parse the SPA-fallback HTML and aborts the whole UI boot. This patch adds ui/studio-api.ts (studioUrl prefixes runtime paths with import.meta.env.BASE_URL; standalone base \"/\" keeps the exact upstream URLs) and routes all 13 URL construction sites through it. No server/start changes (0001/0002 surfaces stay as-is); auth/write-back/CAS semantics unchanged - requests still traverse nginx auth_request -> broker interception -> Java changesets. EXTENDED (C107F3-11): the localization and feedback plugin middlewares install before the studio plugin (start.ts plugin order), so base-path /__studio API calls reached them still prefixed and fell through to vite (404) — the same HYPIT_STUDIO_BASE_PATH strip idiom patch 0001 gave server.ts is applied to both; inert unless the env is set. First exposed by the first-ever browser-driven Studio iframe e2e (locales bootstrap 404 -> initializeI18n throws -> blank iframe).",
